Name that one command as the check for the three mutant cases.

findings.claim:
The design says 'Engine stages run as SYSTEM and cannot map the share (error 1312)' and uses this as a reason the SMB-LOOPBACK check is a person's. That generalises the Windows Sandbox's default identity to the engine.

On this PC the engine runs as the interactive user:
- the worktree is under C:\Users\sshub;
- the admin share 'answers this user';
- the default suite ran 870/870, which TempTree would refuse under a system or service profile;
- Q-038 records SL-062 spike#55 running Network=SMB-LOOPBACK 1 of 1 on this machine.

The real bar is policy: New-SmbMapping changes machine state, the stage permission classifier blocks it (CC-006), and the project treats the run as a person's (#120, #136). The conclusion still stands, but the record now carries a false fact. A later slice could design around it, for example by expecting TempTree's system-profile refusal in every engine run.
